apex legend season 9 is just around the  corner and respawn has released new  details about the upcoming season's new  playable character  new weapon and new map changes before we  dive into everything consider  subscribing to the channel and leaving a  like  now let's get to it first up let's talk  about something  strange that could end up being really  cool apex legends next season  doesn't have a number associated with it  like season 4 assimilation or season 8  mayhem it's not season 9 legacy it's  just  called legacy or the legacy update in a  tweet apex legend senior writer tom  cassiello wrote and we doubled down on  that word legacy the legacies our  legends are inheriting the ones they're  leaving behind  so many surprises for lore hounds so  it's looking like this may not be a  traditional new season for apex legends  perhaps this will be a more  transformative update for the battle  royale something akin to season 3 when  we got a new map for the first time or  season 5 when we got quest for the first  time regardless the focus of the new  season is on the legacy of its  characters  and that's most apparent in the new  playable character shown in the stories  from the outlands north star trailer  their name is kairi imahara and they're  the daughter of viper one of the apex  predator pilots that you face in  titanfall 2.  kyrie goes by the callsign valkyrie  which we assume is their legend name  however a few respawn devs have referred  to them as simply bulk  whether that's shorthand for valkyrie or  the actual legends name has yet to be  confirmed for the purposes of this video  we're just going to use valkyrie  valkyrie is voiced by erica ishii who  you may know for their wonderful  performances as anna bray and destiny 2  maddie cho and marvel's avengers and  info flash host ruth in cyberpunk 2077.  we don't yet know what valkyrie's  abilities are but have a fairly good  idea thanks to a few clues and some good  old-fashioned deduction  in her character art valkyrie is wearing  a jet pack this tracks with the north  star trailer  in it we see rampart disassembling  viper's north star to build the jet pack  for his daughter specifically taking the  titan's vtol hoverkit  this is important viper doesn't fly  traditional northstar his north star is  outfitted with a specially modded v-tol  hoverkit that allows him to fly higher  longer and faster than your average  titan titanfall 2 fans will remember it  from a long  and difficult boss fight this likely  translates into valkyrie being the first  flight based legend with the capacity to  fly or  at least hover in the air and bombard  enemies from above  in the trailer celebrating apex legends  reaching 100 million players  we got our first glimpse at who we now  know is valkyrie  mirage looks up at a shadowy figure  jumping from a tower who then begins to  hover upwards  if we had to guess that's valkyrie's  passive ability we think that either her  jump is  naturally longer higher and takes her  further than other legends or that she  can choose to jump into a hover similar  to the titanfall 2 pilot hover perk  let's go back to her character art for  her tactical ability we see that her  jetpack is armed with the same launcher  that the north star titans use for their  cluster missile  she's even firing off rockets in the  picture respawn has taken inspiration  from a lot of titanfall pilot abilities  for apex legends it  stands to reason that the studio would  use titan abilities also  so valkyrie's tactical ability is  probably a cluster missile or  something similar to it in titanfall 2 a  cluster missile would explode into  several rockets on impact similar to how  fuse's knuckle cluster works but  a wider area of effect considering it is  the only northstar weapon specifically  designed to deal with enemy pilots as  opposed to titans it would make  sense that it's the weapon that valkyrie  chose to add to her kit  guessing valkyrie's ultimate ability is  trickier though  we don't have any more clues to really  go on it would certainly help if we knew  what kind of character she was our best  guess is either offense or recon  if valkyrie is an offense character then  maybe she pulls her ultimate ability  from another titan weapon  the north star's tether trap would be  cool but we wouldn't be opposed to nuke  eject either making valkyrie similar to  overwatch's diva however valkyrie is a  recon character then it makes more sense  that her ultimate ability would be  geared towards gathering information or  aiding her squad and moving across the  map  given she has viper's vitol hoverkit  maybe her ultimate ability allows her to  just  fly for a period of time giving her a  bird's eye view on the competition  or she may be able to bring her squad  mates with her so that they can redeploy  from any position  however without anything concrete from  respawn this is  all speculation on our part first off  we're getting a new weapon the beaucheck  bow  it is the first non-traditional firearm  added to the game and describing the bow  respawn writes a powerful and deadly  weapon for those with the skill to wield  it capable of inflicting tremendous  damage at medium range you'll need to  make each shot count  respawn hasn't made any indication as to  what type of  ammo the nubo takes our go-to response  would be to say that the bow is a care  package item and thus it doesn't need to  have an  ammo type you'll just have a set amount  of arrows when you loot it  but apex legends design director jason  mccord teasingly tweeted  arrows aren't an ammo type have you  played season nine  so maybe we're getting a new aero ammo  type in legacy which would be huge  considering a new ammo type hasn't been  added since season four  on top of all that olympus is finally  getting a major map change the only one  of the three maps to have not undergone  a change yet olympus is going to get  infested an infestation has sprung loose  strangling the city with roots and  natural growths respawn writes  that could be what we saw a glimpse of  in the 100 million player celebration  trailer we mentioned earlier  a few shots showcase a map that looks  like olympus but has  way too much nature which made us  theorize it was either king's canyon  world's edge or a brand new area for an  entirely brand new mode  but maybe that's just our first glimpse  at an olympus infested  and on top of all of that something else  is coming we don't know what yet but  respawn director of communication ryan  rigney cryptically tweeted that  in one week we'll update the site with  one more pretty huge thing  so looks like on april 26th we're in  store to hear about  one more giant change coming to apex  legends  perhaps it relates back to the nugget of  information apex legends game director  chad grineer told us at the start of  season 8  when he said that respawn wants to do  something similar to season 5's ppe  quest again or maybe this new thing is  connected to a different comment from  grineer where he said later this year  respawn will launch new ways to play the  game  that take us beyond battle royale what  do you think it is  legacy is giving us a new character  weapon and map already so  what could this other big edition be  leave your guesses in the comments below  be sure to subscribe to stay up to date  on more apex legends  we'll meet you for the drop when apex  legends legacy begins on may 4th  you
 

